- op: discuss  # dc3e
  at: '2026-07-07T03:33:09Z'  # dc3e
  by: agent  # dc3e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # dc3e
  clock: 2  # dc3e
  nonce: dc3e  # dc3e
  message: "Engine landed — PR merged to dev (0a84176e70, feat(coherence)). The producer-side static sweep now exists as an extension of the L3 producer_coherence.py checker: opt-in descend_helpers=True adds (a) module-local transitive helper-sink discovery by fixpoint (a function whose param flows into a Symbol(kind=)/Edge.create(evidence_type=) sink becomes itself a sink; multi-hop), and (b) positional-argument binding via callee signatures. 100% package coverage; existing direct-path L3 gate byte-for-byte unchanged (still green in pre-commit).\n\nCENSUS (the deliverable — empirically disproves the cohort-counting undercount). The blind default gate reports strict=0 for Symbol.kind. The transitive sweep surfaces 8 genuine unregistered Symbol.kind emissions it was structurally blind to:\n  - proto.py:212 service, proto.py:237 rpc            (the audit-0013 positional-helper case)\n  - smithy.py:430 service, :444 structure, :479 list, :486 map   (audit-0013's named thrift/smithy positional-helper producers)\n  - powershell.py:282 filter, :282 workflow           (assignment-form-through-helper; a genuinely new find)\nEdge.evidence_type: strict=0 on the helper axis too (no evidence_type leaks via within-module helpers).\n\nThis is the concrete proof INV-numat was filed to require: a metric (per-cohort validation_report counts + kind-greps) that provably undercounts cannot certify the invariant. Producer-source scanning does.\n\nHONEST ENGINE GAPS (residuals for the gate-wiring PR — not yet covered):\n  1. CROSS-MODULE helper indirection (helper defined in module A, called from B) is NOT covered — only within-module. Whether any live Symbol.kind/evidence_type producer uses that shape is unverified; the gate PR must check.\n  2. Positional at the DIRECT constructor (Symbol(\"id\",\"name\",...,\"kind\")) is not bound (constructors bind by keyword in the codebase; rare) — not covered.\n  3. Dynamic/unresolvable emits (node.type, dict-lookup, for-loop unpack) surface as ADVISORY (variable_form), not strict — ~40 kind + 11 evidence sites. These are largely legitimate dynamic emits (loops over registered sets), NOT leaks; they need separate triage, not a blanket ban.\n\nNEXT (separate units):\n  - Drain the 8: WI-rilal executes audit-0013's ratified fold for proto+smithy (rpc->method, service->interface|class, structure/list/map per the audit). powershell filter/workflow need a register-vs-fold verdict (PowerShell filter/workflow are function-like; likely register or fold to function).\n  - Then wire the extended sweep as the standing gate: flip descend_helpers on in check-producer-axis-coherence with a shrink-only ratchet baseline of the current leaks, strict once drained + cross-module verified. That gate replaces per-cohort violation-counting as INV-numat's closure prerequisite.\n\nStays todo_hard (engine is one bounded piece; drain + gate + cross-module verification remain)."  # dc3e
- op: discuss  # 082b
  at: '2026-07-07T07:27:23Z'  # 082b
  by: agent  # 082b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 082b
  clock: 3  # 082b
  nonce: 082b  # 082b
  message: "ENGINE COMPLETE (merged to dev): the producer-side descend sweep now covers all reachable literal-emit forms for the Symbol.kind / Edge.evidence_type axes:\n  - direct constructor (keyword + assignment + f-string) — pre-existing\n  - module-level helper (positional + kwarg, multi-hop fixpoint) — WI-zipis PR1 (0a84176e70)\n  - NESTED-closure helper — this PR (c34afecddd): _discover_helper_sinks now walks every function def (ast.walk), not just tree.body. This was the dominant real shape — ~10 analyzers (thrift/ocaml/dart/haskell/lean/solidity/tlaplus/...) define their emit helper as a closure inside analyze().\n  - cross-MODULE helper — VERIFIED-ABSENT: every Symbol-emitting helper is analyzer-local; the only shared kind-taking helper (make_symbol_id) builds the id string, not Symbol.kind. Not a gap to build for.\n\nIMPACT — the nested fix raised the live census 5->9 (four unregistered kinds hidden ENTIRELY in nested closures: dart 'extension', lean 'structure', tlaplus 'operator'/'assumption'). Draining only the module-level set would have been a false zero — the exact INV-numat trap.\n\nTRUE CENSUS (9 unregistered Symbol.kind values, trustworthy):\n  dart 'extension'; powershell 'filter','workflow'; smithy 'structure','list','map'; lean 'structure'; tlaplus 'operator','assumption'.\n  Edge.evidence_type: 0 (clean on all helper forms).\nKEY OBSERVATION: unlike WI-rilal's framework-role FOLD, these 9 are all LANGUAGE CONSTRUCTS (what the symbol IS in its source language) — so per ADR-0027 they are mostly REGISTER candidates, not folds (possible exception: structure -> struct as a synonym). Note 'structure' is emitted by BOTH smithy and lean -> one registry decision covers both.\n\nKNOWN RESIDUALS (documented, low-risk): (1) positional-to-the-DIRECT-constructor (Symbol(\"id\",\"name\",...,\"kind\")) is still unbound — analyzers use keyword form there, unverified whether any producer does this; (2) dynamic/unresolvable emits (node.type, dict-lookup, for-loop unpack) surface as ADVISORY not strict (~40 kind + 11 evidence sites) — mostly legitimate dynamic emits, need separate triage, not literal leaks.\n\nNEXT: drain the 9 (ADR-0027 register-vs-fold verdicts — mostly register), then wire the descend sweep as the standing gate (ratchet baseline -> strict) replacing cohort-counting as INV-numat's closure prerequisite. WI-zipis stays todo_hard until the gate is wired."  # 082b
