  message: "GATE WIRED (merged 5c37ca9118) — the producer-side ratchet is now the standing gate, live in BOTH pre-commit (check-producer-axis-coherence) and CI (test_live_tree_producer_axis_ratchet). It runs the full descend-aware sweep (constructor + module + nested helpers) across all three vocab axes and diffs the live unregistered-value set against a committed shrink-only baseline (.ci/producer-axis-coherence-baseline.json). A NEW unregistered value fails; a drained baselined value must be removed. This REPLACES per-cohort validation_report counting as INV-numat's producer-side closure check — the methodology ruling is now materialized.\n\nWI-zipis's MECHANISM is complete (sweep + gate). Remaining to fully close: DRAIN the 8 baselined Symbol.kind values to zero (assumption, extension, filter, list, map, operator, structure, workflow) via ADR-0027 register-vs-fold verdicts + registry/producer changes, removing each from the baseline as it drains. All 8 are language constructs (mostly REGISTER; structure likely FOLD->struct; smithy list/map is a register-vs-fold fork). Once the baseline hits zero, WI-zipis closes and INV-numat's producer-side gate is green with an empty backlog. Staying todo_hard through the drain."  # 86e9
