  message: "DONE — the producer-side axis-leak sweep is built, wired as the standing gate, and its backlog fully drained. Four merged PRs:\n  1. Engine (0a84176e70): transitive helper-sink discovery + positional binding.\n  2. Nested-closure engine completion (c34afecddd): ast.walk over all defs; cross-module verified-absent. Census 5->9 (nested closures hid 4 more).\n  3. Ratchet gate (5c37ca9118): check-producer-axis-coherence + test_live_tree_producer_axis_ratchet run the full descend sweep vs a shrink-only value-keyed baseline. REPLACES per-cohort validation_report counting (the INV-numat methodology ruling, materialized).\n  4. Drain (892043a816, audit-findings 0015): per-value ADR-0027 verdicts for all 8 baselined Symbol.kind values — 7 REGISTERED (dart extension; powershell filter/workflow; tlaplus operator/assumption; smithy list/map) + 1 FOLDED (structure->struct, smithy+lean). WI-rilal earlier drained proto/thrift/smithy rpc/service.\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (live gate, not a proxy): `python3 scripts/check-producer-axis-coherence` returns \"0 new leaks; 0 baselined value(s) pending drain\" (exit 0); the descend-aware census is [] for ALL THREE vocab axes (Symbol.kind / Edge.evidence_type / Edge.edge_type). The sweep is exhaustive by construction: direct constructor + module-level helpers + nested-closure helpers; cross-module helper sinks proven not to exist for these axes (only make_symbol_id crosses modules, and it builds the id string not Symbol.kind). Any new unregistered value now fails pre-commit AND the CI test.\n\nThis is the trustworthy producer-side closure check INV-numat needs — replacing the diagnostic that provably undercounted (the false RESOLVED in audit-0013 that started this)."  # 0a63
